# The wheel drives the pane the pointer is over, and only that one.
#
# Splitting shows two transcripts at once, each with its own scroll view and its
# own follow-latch (PaneState is keyed by pane index as well as thread id). The
# thing that goes wrong when a second pane arrives is that a gesture keeps
# addressing the first one -- the scroll views used to share a debug name, and
# the follow-latch used to share a map key -- so the claim worth holding is not
# "the wheel works" but "the wheel works on the one under the pointer".
#
# The right pane holds the long thread and the left holds a short one, so
# "#39:" is text that exists in the RIGHT pane and nowhere else on screen. Its
# disappearance is the right pane having scrolled, and its survival is the left
# pane's wheel not having reached across.
#
# Note the right pane's transcript is a shorter slice than the same thread
# opened alone -- the split-open path loads fewer messages -- so this asserts on
# the newest message, which is loaded either way, rather than on the oldest.
#
# The panes are 280..688 and 693..1100 at this window size (measured with
# `assert_ui transcript_scroll x=…` and `assert_ui transcript_scroll_2 x=…`), so
# 400 is inside the left one and 900 inside the right. Coordinates because the
# runner has no element-addressed pointer move (afterhours_gaps.md #285).
#
# NOTE: expect_no_text takes a BARE single word — see afterhours_gaps.md #47.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_BIG_TRANSCRIPT=1 HANABI_OPEN=t2 HANABI_SPLIT=rbig

# Both panes open pinned to their newest message. Both preconditions are
# stated: require_thread asks every pane, so this holds that the split really
# is t2 on the left and rbig on the right before a single wheel event.
require_thread t2
require_thread rbig
wait_frames 20
expect_text "Follow-up question #39:"

# 1. The wheel over the LEFT pane does not reach across the divider.
mouse_move 400 400
wait_frames 5
scroll_wheel 0 40
wait_frames 25
expect_text "Follow-up question #39:"

# 2. The wheel over the RIGHT pane scrolls the right pane.
mouse_move 900 400
wait_frames 5
scroll_wheel 0 40
wait_frames 25
expect_no_text #39:
